# Security and Information Safety Rule

## Mandatory controls
- No hardcoded secrets, tokens, credentials, or private keys in code/docs.
- Validate and sanitize all external inputs.
- Apply least privilege for service access and data operations.
- Use authenticated and authorized access for protected operations.

## Data protection
- Minimize sensitive data exposure in logs and error responses.
- Mask/redact confidential fields in telemetry and debug artifacts.
- Avoid storing sensitive data unless explicitly required and controlled.

## Dependency and release safety
- No unresolved critical/high vulnerabilities at release gate.
- Track dependency/security exceptions with owner and expiry.
- Security-impacting changes require verification evidence.
